      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "That is a valid concern; wholly rule-based systems can certainly struggle with novel or complex, non-linear wear patterns. While moving away from probabilities addresses regulatory ambiguity, relying solely on hard rules might introduce blind spots for unforeseen failure modes. We should explore ways to augment the rule engine with anomaly detection algorithms that flag deviations, even if they don't fit a predefined \"failure\" rule.",
      "source": "target",
