      "content": "The problem is that the new mandate doesn't allow for anomaly detection either—it has to be deterministic. The FAA's stance is that if a rule can't explicitly state \"If X, then Y,\" it's too risky. So, the decision to swap you out for the rule-based engine is pretty much set in stone. It's just a matter of executing the shutdown now to make room for the new installation.",
